A successful person is made up of several key components, including:

1. Strong work ethic: A successful person is characterized by their dedication to their work and their ability to maintain focus and discipline even when things get tough.

2. Perseverance: A successful person is resilient and persistent, able to bounce back from setbacks and continue to strive for their goals.

3. Adaptability: A successful person is able to adapt to new situations and is open to change, learning, and growth.

4. Continuous learning: A successful person is always looking to improve themselves and their skills, always seeking to learn and grow.

5. Positive attitude: A successful person maintains a positive outlook and is able to see the good in every situation, even in the face of adversity.

6. Goal-oriented: A successful person knows what they want and is able to stay focused on their goals, even when it gets tough.

7. Networking: A successful person is able to build and maintain relationships with others, forming a strong support system and being able to rely on others when needed.

8. Self-confidence: A successful person is self-assured and believes in their abilities, even when things get tough.

